[h1]Filters & Surfaces Cheat Sheet[/h1]

[h2]Built-in Item Filters[/h2]

Pass these as the [b]enabled[/b] field. All are pcall-safe — if PZ renames an API method, the filter returns false and logs a warning instead of crashing your mod.

[code]
local F = TooltipLib.Filters

F.weapon         -- any HandWeapon (melee or ranged)
F.melee          -- melee only
F.firearm        -- ranged only (guns, bows)
F.clothing       -- clothing and armor
F.food           -- food items
F.container      -- bags, backpacks
F.fluidContainer -- water bottles, gas cans
F.drainable      -- batteries, lighters
F.literature     -- books and magazines
F.skillBook      -- skill XP books only
F.recipeBook     -- recipe-teaching books only
F.key            -- keys
F.stackable      -- ammo, nails, etc.
F.medical        -- bandages, pills
[/code]

[h2]World Object Filters[/h2]

[code]
F.generator      -- IsoGenerator
F.rainCollector  -- rain barrels
F.farmPlant      -- farm plants
[/code]

[h2]Filter Factories[/h2]

[code]
F.customType("Base.Axe")           -- specific item type
F.instanceof("Literature")         -- Java class check
F.hasTag("COOKABLE")               -- script tag
F.displayCategory("SkillBook")     -- display category
F.objectSprite("appliances_01_0")  -- world object sprite
F.inRange(3)                       -- within N tiles of player
[/code]

[h2]Combining Filters[/h2]

[code]
-- Both must pass
enabled = F.allOf(F.clothing, F.container)

-- Either passes
enabled = F.anyOf(F.weapon, F.clothing)

-- Invert
enabled = F.negate(F.food)

-- Custom logic on top of a filter
local isWeaponOrClothing = F.anyOf(F.weapon, F.clothing)
enabled = function(item)
    if not isWeaponOrClothing(item) then return false end
    return myCustomCheck(item)
end,
[/code]

[b]Tip:[/b] Pre-compose combinators outside the function. Don't create new allOf/anyOf inside enabled() — that allocates a closure every hover frame.

[h2]The Six Surfaces[/h2]

[b]Layout surfaces[/b] (item, itemSlot, object) — use PZ's ObjectTooltip layout. Aligned columns. Support addTexture/addTextureRow.

[b]Rich text surfaces[/b] (skill, vehicle) — append to ISToolTip via rich text markup. Progress bars render as colored percentage text.

[b]Recipe surface[/b] — uses a RecipeContentPanel. Full visual progress bars. Access raw ISTableLayout via ctx.rootTable if needed.

All six share the same add* methods. Your callback code is portable across surfaces.

[code]
-- Item tooltip
target = "item"      -- enabled(item),        ctx.item
target = "itemSlot"  -- enabled(item),        ctx.item

-- World object
target = "object"    -- enabled(object, sq),  ctx.object, ctx.square

-- Rich text
target = "skill"     -- enabled(perk, level), ctx.perk, ctx.level, ctx.player
target = "vehicle"   -- enabled(part, veh),   ctx.part, ctx.vehicle

-- Recipe
target = "recipe"    -- enabled(recipe),      ctx.recipe, ctx.logic, ctx.player
[/code]
